  "meta": {
    "title": "2026-06-09-post-mortem-visuals · candidate-005 (chat section spec)"
  },
  "agent": {
    "note": "Iter 5 — drilling into the chat section per your direction. Canvas restricted to chat dimensions (768x1080 = 40% of 1920x1080). Sample bubbles via placeRects: agent (left, 73% width), human (right, 73%), system (centered, 50%). Stacked top-to-bottom with constant 20px gap. Bubble height 100px (60px for system separator). Each rect labeled via stableKey M0Label so you can comment on per-bubble decisions: y-spacing, max x-depth, bubble height, agent-vs-human width parity. Width-only fix in this round; per-speaker tint colors are on the labels but the rect fills are uniform — real bubble styling comes after spacing approval. Also fixed the editor label overflow (fitLabelFontSize in FileDetailsModal + PackOverview).",
    "question": "How does the y-spacing feel? Bubbles too tall / too short / well-spaced? Max x-depth (73%) leaves room for an avatar / sender icon — too narrow? Should system separators be even smaller? Agent and human currently mirror each other in width — keep that symmetry or differentiate?",
    "context": {
      "category": {
        "kind": "known",
        "value": "spacing-alignment"
      },
      "intent": {
        "action": "refine",
        "summary": "spec sample chat bubbles for y-spacing + x-depth review"
      },
      "relation": {
        "kind": "refines",
        "target": "004"
      },
      "layoutIntent": "free"
    },
    "response": {
      "body": "agent and human boxes generally look good. can we split them into the areas for avatars as well so I can see the intended spacing? I'd also like to see the system:candidate-002 take up much more width. I think system notes can be a lighter font and take the whole width because they arent from either \"side\"",
      "from": "human",
      "at": "2026-06-10T02:42:21.562Z"
    }
  },
  "size": {
    "width": 768,
    "height": 1080
  },
